From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 19:13:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] PS5: thread ids, names, affinity, signals and fibers

What the console exports, from the payload SDK's stub libraries:

- Thread ids: pthread_getthreadid_np (no SYS_gettid); a thread records its
  own as it starts, since pthread_t is a pointer.
- Names: pthread_set_name_np is libkernel's (pthread_setname_np is only in a
  module a title does not load, and no header declares pthread_getname_np),
  so the thread keeps the name it was given.
- Affinity: the platform layer's ps5_pthread_{get,set}affinity_np, since
  FreeBSD's 32-byte cpuset_t gets ERANGE from the console's own calls.
- Suspend and callback wakeups: SIGUSR1/SIGUSR2 with pthread_kill, the macOS
  path. There is no pthread_sigqueue, FreeBSD's sigqueue aims at a process,
  and realtime signal delivery to a thread is unproven on the console.
- Fibers: getcontext, makecontext and swapcontext are exported, and the SDK
  fork's ucontext_t matches the console's layout.

Untested on a console: EdgeOfTimeRecomp's ps5/probe checks these.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_0136zBnRC7dbQro6PQoycWYT
